+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-18-reject-sparse-patch/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+## Context
+
+`applyPatch` builds its operations with `patch.map(parseOperation)`, and `Array.prototype.map` skips holes, so a sparse patch is partly ignored.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+- Holes are reported as `InvalidPatchError`.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+- Any other change to validation or operation semantics (checked against RFC 6902; no other deviation found).
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Replace `map` with an index loop over `patch.length`, which visits holes as `undefined`; `parseOperation` already rejects non-objects with `InvalidPatchError`.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- None; dense arrays behave as before.
diff --git a/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-18-reject-sparse-patch/proposal.md b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-18-reject-sparse-patch/proposal.md
