--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-18-reject-sparse-patch/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+## Why
+
+`applyPatch` silently skips holes in a patch array (e.g. `[op, , op]`) or, when the hole is the only thing it reaches, can fail with a raw `TypeError`. A malformed patch must be reported as an invalid patch (RFC 6902 §3: a patch is an array of operation objects).
+
+## What Changes
+
+- A patch array with a missing element (hole) is rejected with `InvalidPatchError`, like any other non-object element.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `json-patch`: invalid-patch requirement now covers holes in the patch array.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/patch.ts` validation and `src/patch.test.ts`; no API change.
